---
description: Guidelines for creating effective Cursor rule files
globs: ".cursor/rules/**/*.mdc"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Modular: one concern per file, not monolithic
- `globs` (plural) for file-scoped rules; comma-separated string or YAML array
- `alwaysApply: true` only for true globals; omit globs then
- Target under 50 lines; patterns and conventions, not verbose examples; no h1
- Do not `@`-attach MDX or `apps/docu/` from rules. Do not `@` files from `alwaysApply` rules
- `@` another `.mdc` only if you intend to attach that small rule and it is not already always-on
- Do not use description-only “apply intelligently” rules — those belong in skills
